1 | fences | Baker (22nd North Carolina): a run was made for the fence and over it, across the road to the stone fence, which was jumped on the way to the top of Cemetery Ridge | - | 1863-07-03 (a veteran's later recollection reprinted in the lesson; hedged) | hedged | The lesson reprints Baker's recollection that a run was made for the fence and over it, that he was shot down about halfway across the road, and that the rest of the command jumped the stone fence and charged to the top of Cemetery Ridge | at which time a run was made for the fence and over it. >>> rushed on and jumped the stone fence, charging rapidly to the top of Cemetery Ridge | Andrew Baker was a soldier in the 22nd North Carolina Infantry, C.S.A., Pettigrew's brigade.
1 | buildings | Baker (22nd North Carolina): a little house against which the end of the stone fence rested on either side | - | 1863-07-03 (a veteran's later recollection reprinted in the lesson; the house is not named; hedged) | hedged | The lesson reprints Baker's recollection of a little house, just against which the end of the stone fence rested on either side, behind which some ten or twelve men of the Twenty-sixth North Carolina halted for a moment | Just after I had fallen I looked to my right, where a little house stood >>> halted, with Capt. W. T. Magruder | Andrew Baker was a soldier in the 22nd North Carolina Infantry, C.S.A., Pettigrew's brigade.
